  "img": "systems/draw-steel/assets/classes/tactician.png",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You are the crew's voice and its will. Where the Operator wins the firefight and the Hacker owns the net, you win the <em>room</em> and direct the fight without firing a shot. Corp records call you a liaison, talent, or handler; the street calls you the <strong>Face</strong>, the <strong>boss</strong>, or simply the one who does the talking.</p><p>Your engine is <strong>Influence</strong>: social-and-tactical fuel, earned by leading well and spent to grant allies extra actions, movement, and edges, and to bend scenes, negotiations, and NPCs to the crew's advantage. Low personal damage; high impact <em>through other people</em>.</p><h3>The Influence Engine (live, not banked)</h3><ul><li><strong>Command cadence:</strong> at the start of each of your turns in combat, gain Influence (benchmark ~1-2/turn).</li><li><strong>Take the lead:</strong> the first turn each encounter, gain bonus Influence equal to your <strong>Victories</strong>.</li><li><strong>Successful direction:</strong> when a directed ally lands a Tier-1 result, or you win a key negotiation exchange, gain extra Influence.</li><li><strong>Reading the room:</strong> a successful Insight read on a foe/NPC grants a small Influence bonus.</li></ul><p><strong>Cap by Hero Tier (T5 to T1): 4 / 6 / 8 / 10 / 12.</strong> Unused Influence is <strong>lost at the end of the encounter or scene</strong> - authority is momentary. Signature abilities cost no Influence; heroic abilities spend it. Influence is class power on the BP side of the firewall - never bought or fed by nuyen or Body Integrity.</p><h3>Advancement (internal Level 1-5 = player-facing Tier 5-1)</h3><p>At <strong>Tier 5</strong> you choose your subclass (Corp-Exec / Street-Fixer / Bard), gain all three signatures, and pick an opening heroic. Every Tier after, you gain a new heroic ability, your Influence cap rises, and your Presence/Insight sharpen. The ladder caps at <strong>Tier 1</strong>.</p>",
      "director": ""
    },
